{{fbdoc item="title" value="SDL, the Simple DirectMedia Layer"}}----
Cross-platform mulitmedia library

Website: http://www.libsdl.org
Platforms supported: ""Win32"", Linux, FreeBSD, Haiku (SDL 1.2)
Headers to include: SDL/SDL.bi or SDL2/SDL.bi
Header version: SDL 1.2.15, SDL2 2.0.3
Examples: yes, in examples/graphics/SDL1/, examples/graphics/SDL2/, and examples/graphics/SDL3/

FreeBSD runtime checks passed for SDL 3 core, image, TrueType and network
examples, plus the SDL 1.2 video-info example under Xvfb. SDL 2 runtime, audio
devices and physical display behavior remain unqualified.

Haiku R1 beta 6 amd64: `examples/graphics/SDL1/core/video_info.bas` compiled and
ran with FreeBASIC 1.20.4-3 against HaikuPorts SDL 1.2.15. This headless check
covered SDL initialization and video-info queries; it did not open a window or
test rendering. SDL 2 and SDL 3 remain unqualified on Haiku.

